sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-sweep.yaml, docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#sweep-task-vm-hosts, #report-strays and #sweep-upcloud, docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (second pass), rules 14 (no `format` or `result` steps and no root `format`; the Gateway reads each plan step and the run's step statuses), 9 (one read-back and one native `assert` per provider), 18 (one workflow; the inventory reads are one forEach, removals parallel forEach, server and template deletes one forEach), 21 (a `guard` runs only the admitted provider's steps; the provider children are folded in, they were no typed boundary), 11 (removal behaviors keep a per-host index name: a name per VM would leave one definition per VM ever swept, Lab #4280).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · scheduled host sweep every 30 minutes
  %% kind: task_vm.sweep_host
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane UC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  participant UC as UpCloud API<br/>HTTPS from 209
  Note over GW: Admit the sweep<br/>host Node 13 · task #5182
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `SweepTaskVmHosts`, queued every 30 minutes while task VMs are on or the UpCloud token is set
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no open sweep of Node 13; the generic Operation lock holds the host until the terminal result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the ownership scope: live VM names, maximum VM and build ids, project, pool, operator-owned names, recorded, retired and protected builds
  %%> - retires expired builds before dispatch; logs stray records and stray Nodes from its own state
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-sweep
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `operation_id`, `node_id` 13, `kind`, the full public `intent` with provider and scope
  %%> - for Incus, Node 13's address, user and pinned SSH host key
  %%> - for UpCloud, the vault key name `task-vm-upcloud-token` only (R3)
  %%> How:
  %%> - one workflow; a `guard` on each provider's first step skips the other provider, and its later steps skip with it
  alt Incus host
    SW->>H: Read the inventory<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 3
    %%> How:
    %%> - three parallel pinned `@swamp/ssh exec` argv: `sudo timeout 60 incus query` for instances of all projects, custom volumes of the pool, and images of the project
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - a missing project fails the image read, so the host changes nothing
    Note over SW: Plan the removals<br/>plan · task-vm-sweep-input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - TypeScript on 209 selects orphaned `tvm-<n>` VMs, eligible image builders and smoke VMs, and orphaned seed clones, within the captured id limits
    %%> - logs one warning per stray instance, stray volume and stray record; strays are never removed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the planned names, the deleted names and the names that stay, which the Gateway reads
    SW->>H: Remove orphaned VMs<br/>remove-instance · forEach
    %%> How:
    %%> - `sudo timeout 180 incus delete --force --project orbit-tasks -- <name>`, one item per VM, in parallel
    SW->>H: Remove orphaned volumes<br/>remove-volume · forEach
    %%> How:
    %%> - `incus storage volume delete` for each `tvm-<n>-topology-seed` clone whose VM is gone, after the VMs
    SW->>H: Read the project again<br/>ssh exec · incus query
    %%> How:
    %%> - `incus query /1.0/instances?project=orbit-tasks`
    SW->>SW: Check the VMs are gone<br/>assert
    %%> End check:
    %%> - a native `assert`: no planned VM name is in the read-back
  else UpCloud
    SW->>UC: List servers, templates<br/>inventory · curl on 209
    %%> How:
    %%> - one inline `curl` per list, the token through `--variable`, never argv: servers labelled `orbit-task-vm` and `orbit-task-image`, and storage templates
    Note over SW: Plan the cloud removals<br/>plan · task-vm-sweep-input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - selects servers without a live row, build servers and unverified templates older than two hours, except a build still marked running
    SW->>UC: Stop started servers<br/>stop-server · forEach
    %%> How:
    %%> - a hard stop per started server, in parallel
    SW->>UC: Delete servers, templates<br/>remove · forEach
    %%> How:
    %%> - one parallel `forEach`: each server with its storage, each unverified template
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - UpCloud refuses a server that is still stopping; the next sweep deletes it
    SW->>UC: List again<br/>inventory · curl on 209
    %%> How:
    %%> - the same three lists
    SW->>SW: Check the cloud removals<br/>assert
    %%> End check:
    %%> - a native `assert`: no planned server or template UUID is still listed
  end
  alt sweep complete
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run once; it takes the plan step's names
    Note over GW: Project the sweep<br/>missing VMs · build claims
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a `ready` or `parked` VM missing on two sweeps in a row becomes `failed` with `task_vm.vm_missing`, and its group asks for assistance
    %%> - a failed build's cleanup claim is released when none of its names remain
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the sweep failed<br/>no missing-VM count
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5182 fails with `task_vm.host_command_failed`
    %%> - a provider or SSH failure never counts as a missing VM; build claims stay; the next sweep runs again in 30 minutes
  end
